Spis desktop names why its corpus location or a backend answer could not be read

The corpus configuration (~/.config/spis/corpus.json) was read with try?,
so a file that could not be read, was not JSON, had another schema or
named no root made the app say no corpus was configured; the app screen
and the manage screen now show which file failed and why, and 'Spis data
could not be loaded' carries the index's cause.

Refusals whose body was not a JSON envelope showed 'The request failed.
Try again.'; they now carry the HTTP status and body. A stream line that
was not a JSON event was skipped, so a damaged result line ended as
'closed early'; it now fails the operation naming the line. The build
profile list became the BuildProfile enum and the client's error type
moved to SpisClient+Wire.swift.

Repairs: "Manage names a catalog index or references file it cannot read" Manage read the corpus root with a locate that could not say why a location was unreadable; it now reads it through locatedRoot, which names the cause
Repairs: "feat(manage): edit reference metadata without replacing evidence" the client's error type it extended moved to SpisClient+Wire.swift with the refusal sentence and stream event readers

